From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: keep the LEDs in an array

b43 keeps one LED per trigger (TX, RX, radio and association) and reads
the behaviour of GPIO pins 0-3 from the SPROM. A second LED with the
same function got -EEXIST and was not registered.

Keep the LEDs in an array, up to two per pin, so that an activity LED
can take the TX and the RX trigger on one pin and several pins can have
the same function. Leave a pin alone when the SPROM describes no LED on
it. b43_leds_gpio_mask() and b43_leds_gpio_activelow() report the pins
the LEDs use, for the GPIO setup of the AC-PHY cores in a later patch,
which also reads pins 4-15 from the NVRAM of those boards.

On the other cores, a second LED of one function now registers instead
of failing with -EEXIST; pins 0-3 keep their SPROM behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
